{
  "title": "Adult Respiratory Distress Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1006/adult-respiratory-distress-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 27 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Adult respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) is a pulmonary condition that can arise after polytrauma and long bone fractures leading to acute lung injury and progressive respiratory distress, refractory hypoxemia and pulmonary edema.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made in the polytrauma patient by calculation of hypoxemia defined by PaO2 / FIO2 ratio < 200 mm Hg with chest x-ray revealing diffuse bilateral pulmonary infiltrates with pulmonary edema.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is focused on prevention with early stabilization of long bone fractures and PEEP ventilation when ARDS develops.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**acute endothelial damage resulting from**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**aspiration**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**infection**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**pancreatitis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**multiple blood transfusions**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**lung injury**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**sepsis or shock**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**major trauma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**large surface area burns**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fat emboli",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "thromboembolism",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "multi-system organ failure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "injury cascade leads to",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**respiratory distress**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**refractory hypoxemia**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**decreased lung compliance**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "ARDS is represented by three phases",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 4,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**3 phases of ARDS**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "*Exudative phase*",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Initially",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Hyaline membrane comprised of fibrin form",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "*Proliferative phase*",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "3 days",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Alveolar exudate resolves or organizes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1006/images/ards.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "*Fibrotic phase*",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "3-4 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Alveolar ducts and spaces undergo fibrosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "acute onset (12-48 hours) of",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**dyspnea**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fever",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**mottled or cyanotic skin**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**resistant hypoxia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "intercostal retractions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "rales/crackles and ronchi",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "tachypnea",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Evaluation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Hypoxemia is refractory to O2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "3 different categories of ARDS based on degree of hypoxemia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "PaO2 / FIO2 ratio < 300 mm Hg= mild",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "classified as acute lung injury (ALI)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "PaO2 / FIO2 ratio < 200 mm Hg= moderate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "values below 200 classified as ARDS",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "PaO2 / FIO2 ratio < 100 mm Hg= severe",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Chest xray",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "shows patchy pulmonary edema (air space disease)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "diffuse **bilateral pulmonary infiltrates**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "normal sized heart",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "makes CHF less likely",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Respiratory compliance (<40 mL/cm H20)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Positive end-expiratory pressure (>10cm H20)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Corrected expired volume per minute (>10L/min)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Cardiogenic pulmonary edema (i.e. CHF or MI), bilateral pneumonia, SARS",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "PEEP ventilation and steroids",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "treat the underlying pathology/disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "early stabilization of long bone fractures (femur)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prevention",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closely monitor PEEP in patients at-risk of ARDS",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "serial X-rays in concerning patients can assist in early identification and intervention",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Pneumothorax**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "secondary to ventilator with high PEEP",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "High mortality rate (50% overall) is associated with ARDS even in setting of ICU",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
